{'symbol': 'PHM', 'date': '2020-04-23 11:30:00', 'title': 'Pultegroup Says Seeing Minimal Cancellation From Most Buyers - Conf Call', 'text': 'PULTEGROUP SAYS POSTPONING PURCHASING LAND PARCELS CURRENTLY UNDER CONTRACT- CONF CALL.PULTEGROUP SAYS SEEING MINIMAL CANCELLATION FROM MOST BUYERS- CONF CALL.PULTEGROUP SAYS MARCH 2020 ORDERS FELL 11% VERSUS A YEAR AGO- CONF CALL.PULTEGROUP SAYS CO IS LEVERAGING TECHNOLOGY TO ENABLE VIRTUAL INTERACTIONS WITH HOMEBUYERS.PULTEGROUP SAYS HOMEBUYERS ARE WALKING COMPUTER GENERATED FLOOR PLANS AND PICKING A LOT ON CO’S INTERACTIVE COMMUNITY MAPS AND APPLYING FOR MORTGAGE.PULTEGROUP SAYS OPERATIONS OF PULTE MORTGAGE HAVE CONTINUED WITH MINIMAL INTERRUPTION.PULTEGROUP SAYS MAJORITY OF BUYERS IN CO’S BACKLOG MADE A BUYING DECISION PRIOR TO COVID-19, AND MOST OF THEM ARE READY TO MOVE TO THE CLOSING TABLE.PULTEGROUP SAYS TO DATE SOLD 900 HOMES IN APRIL THROUGH VIRTUAL TRANSACTIONS.PULTEGROUP SAYS THROUGH THE FIRST 3 WEEKS OF APRIL, CO HAD 360 BACKLOG UNITS CANCELED, WHICH REPRESENTS 3% OF HOMES IN BACKLOG.PULTEGROUP SAYS BUYER DESIRE TO OWN A HOME IS HOLDING STRONG, AND THERE HASN’T BEEN A LOT OF DISCOUNTING ON THE HOME PRICING.PULTEGROUP SAYS "UNDERLYING TREND IS THAT BUYER TRAFFIC TO OUR WEBSITE, AND IN TURN, OUR COMMUNITIES HAS DECREASED MATERIALLY".'}
